    <briefdescription>
<para>Utility to embed an integer into a pointer-like type. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This is specifically intended to allow embedding integers where fewer bits are required than exist in a pointer, and the integer can participate in abstractions along side other pointer-like types. For example it can be placed into a <computeroutput><ref refid="classllvm_1_1_pointer_sum_type" kindref="compound">PointerSumType</ref></computeroutput> or <computeroutput><ref refid="classllvm_1_1_pointer_union" kindref="compound">PointerUnion</ref></computeroutput>.</para>
<para>Note that much like pointers, an integer value of zero has special utility due to boolean conversions. For example, a non-null value can be tested for in the above abstractions without testing the particular active member. Also, the default constructed value zero initializes the integer. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
